{
  "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
  "total_duration_s": 72.7667,
  "total_frames_30fps": 2183,
  "segments": [
    {
      "seg_id": "N01",
      "text": "In Antarctica's freezing Dry Valleys, a five-story waterfall pours blood-red straight out of solid glacier ice.",
      "rate": "+3%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 0.1,
      "end": 6.503,
      "duration": 6.403,
      "pause_after": 0.22,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N02",
      "text": "For decades, nobody knew what fed Taylor Glacier's Blood Falls. Today, we know the color comes from chemistry: salty, iron-rich water hits the air and instantly rusts.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 6.723,
      "end": 17.236,
      "duration": 10.514,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N03",
      "text": "Deep under the ice sits a trapped reservoir of hyper-salty brine\u2014likely ancient seawater sealed off as the glacier advanced, though its full history remains under investigation.",
      "rate": "+0%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 17.496,
      "end": 26.887,
      "duration": 9.39,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N04",
      "text": "Rust explains the color. What surprised researchers in 2026 was what they pulled from the freezing red mud.",
      "rate": "+2%",
      "pitch": "+1Hz",
      "start": 27.167,
      "end": 33.723,
      "duration": 6.556,
      "pause_after": 0.24,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N05",
      "text": "Testing 167 ice, sediment, air, and ocean samples across the region, a field team uncovered a hidden community of marine microbes right at the red outflow.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 33.963,
      "end": 43.73,
      "duration": 9.767,
      "pause_after": 0.25,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N06",
      "text": "Under the microscope were tiny ocean algae like diatoms, alongside single-celled marine drifters\u2014living clues of past ocean connections, miles from open sea.",
      "rate": "+0%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 43.98,
      "end": 53.195,
      "duration": 9.215,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N07",
      "text": "Now, that doesn't prove these exact organisms stayed trapped beneath the ice for millions of years. Scientists are still piecing together how they got there.",
      "rate": "-2%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 53.475,
      "end": 62.463,
      "duration": 8.988,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N08",
      "text": "Blood Falls isn't bleeding. It's a leaking subglacial vault\u2014showing that even beneath 400 meters of Antarctic ice, Earth holds unexpected signs of life.",
      "rate": "-1%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 62.743,
      "end": 72.479,
      "duration": 9.736,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    }
  ],
